# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage outputs
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
fuzz/
.testkit/
# Rapid failfiles under testdata/rapid/ are committed for auto-replay
# regression. Only ignore rapid/ at the repo root (build artifacts).
!/testdata/rapid/
!**/testdata/rapid/

# ...except those written by a stand-in TB. Negative tests drive a rapid
# property that is *meant* to fail, inside a testkit.FailableTB that captures
# the failure instead of propagating it. rapid still writes a failfile, named
# for the TB, on every green run — and replaying one only reproduces a failure
# the test asked for. They carry no regression value, regenerate under a new
# timestamped name each run, and have been committed by accident before.
#
# The directory is named for the TB, so this only catches stand-ins left at the
# default name. A negative rapid test using WithName writes elsewhere and needs
# its own entry — or, better, should not rename the TB.
**/testdata/rapid/FailableTB/
coverage.txt
coverage.html
profile.out

